This repository contains third-party data and data computed with third-party
software. Each item below says what it is, where it came from and its terms.


1. MUIS prayer timetable (MosqueBoard example)

File: Examples/MosqueBoard/MosqueBoard/Timetables/muis-2026.json

Contains information from Muslim Prayer Timetable 2026 accessed on 2026-10-13
from data.gov.sg (Majlis Ugama Islam Singapura) which is made available under
the terms of the Singapore Open Data Licence version 1.0
https://data.gov.sg/open-data-licence

The data was converted to SalahKit's timetable format by
Examples/MosqueBoard/Scripts/convert-muis.py. This file is covered by the
Singapore Open Data Licence, not by this repository's MIT License. Neither MUIS
nor data.gov.sg endorses this project, and the example doesn't present the data
as an official MUIS product.


2. Times computed with Adhan Swift (SalahFixtures and MosqueBoard example)

Files: the timetable data in Sources/SalahFixtures, and
Examples/MosqueBoard/MosqueBoard/Timetables/edinburgh-synthetic.json

The prayer times in the SalahFixtures sample data and the begin times in the
synthetic Edinburgh timetable were computed with Adhan Swift
(https://github.com/batoulapps/adhan-swift, commit a6fa2de), used as a
calculator on a development machine. Adhan Swift is Copyright (c) 2016 Batoul
Apps and is distributed under the MIT License. This repository contains none of
Adhan Swift's code. Sources/SalahFixtures/FixtureData.md and
Examples/MosqueBoard/Timetables.md record how the times were made.
